# Always use gh

SSH to `git@github.com` fails on this machine (`Permission denied (publickey)`). Never `git push`, `git pull`, or `git fetch` over the `origin` SSH URL.

- Issues, PRs, checks, releases, and GitHub API: `gh` only.
- Push/pull/fetch: HTTPS with a one-shot `gh` credential helper. Do **not** run `gh auth setup-git` or change git config.

```bash
# ✅ push current branch
git -c credential.helper='!f() { echo "username=x-access-token"; echo "password=$(gh auth token)"; }; f' \
  push https://github.com/RecursiveTrail/three-js-experiement.git HEAD

# ✅ update origin/main tracking after a push
git -c credential.helper='!f() { echo "username=x-access-token"; echo "password=$(gh auth token)"; }; f' \
  fetch https://github.com/RecursiveTrail/three-js-experiement.git main:refs/remotes/origin/main

# ❌ BAD
git push origin main
git pull
ssh git@github.com
```
